[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_5bs2s")
fish_name = "Please I Need Fish"
grade = 2
sprite = ExtResource("2_lqp4u")
catch_blurb = "Why is it trying not to laugh?"
description = "This fish lies in a perpetual social stalemate. Regardless of the subject matter, it will always find itself holding in what leading theories assume to be laughter. Should it laugh, the lifeform in front of it will get upset. Should it try to respond, it will laugh. Out of self-interest, it sits in a happy medium.

One of the earliest hyper-intelligent aquatic species, it was historically sought after for its wisdom. However, the long lifespans of these lifeforms means that, at some point, they will have heard it all! A fish whose mother is kind of reefless, a starfish who has stuffed all of their clams in one basket...the list goes on. The contortion of their expression at the slightest of troubles has soiled the once glorious reputation of this species’ infinite wisdom. Many now consider these fish disrespectful.

The only ailments a Please I Need Fish can earnestly listen to these days are those of its own kind: the dissatisfaction of solving the same problems over again, and that no matter how intelligent the species, they seem to never learn. When a Please I Need Fish cannot find others like it to rant to, it will often lean on the comforting presence of the Moai Fish.

Their name originates from the pleas of those seeking their species’ wisdom. With the loss of its reputation and cultural significance, some newly-arising colloquial names for the fish are “Who Is Fish” and “Kiss Fish.”
"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cr3nmjdvpgh0a"
